  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Saturday) \nIssued at 1007 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nSurface high pressure by the mid week should be situated over the\ncoastal Mid Atlantic region. An anticyclonic flow rounding the\nwestern periphery of this high will bring a SE flow across the Deep\nSouth, and help continue a gradual warming trend. Despite the days\ngetting shorter progressing trough the autumn, above normal warmth\nshould continue for the mid and latter portions of the new week.\nHighs on Wed should rise into the low/mid 80s under generally sunny\nskies. Temperatures should creep up a tad both Thu and Fri, with\nhighs on Fri in the mid/upper 80s. Lows Wed and Thu night should\nrange from the mid/upper 40s in those normally cooler locations, to\nthe mid 50s near large bodies of water. Normal high/low temperatures \nby Fri, Oct 9th are around 79/55.\n\nThe SE flow will gradually bring more moisture and clouds inland \nfrom the Gulf region was we near the weekend. Enough of this moisture\nreturn will also bring lower end rain chances back to the Tennessee\nValley - right in time for the next upcoming weekend. The moisture\nshould make for somewhat milder conditions Fri night with lows in the\n50s, and highs on Sat with rain chances in the low/mid 80s.",
